# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A toml/ini fence closes on its own closer, whatever the embedded grammar holds open"

# The fence's `while` guard is checked once per line, before the embedded grammar's own scan
# runs on that line — so a construct the embedded grammar leaves open (an unterminated triple
# quote, an unclosed array, an unclosed inline table) never reaches past the closing fence. Each
# case below opens one such construct and never closes it, then closes the FENCE, then carries an
# ordinary sentence. The sentence must carry only paragraph ground: nothing from `toml` or `ini`.

```toml
key = """an unterminated triple-quoted string
```

An ordinary sentence after the unterminated triple-quote.
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

```toml
key = [1, 2,
```

An ordinary sentence after the unclosed array.
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

```toml
key = { a = 1,
```

An ordinary sentence after the unclosed inline table.
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

```ini
[section
key = value
```

An ordinary sentence after an unterminated ini section header.
#<- text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5
